---
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { lastUpdatedIso } from '../config/pages';
import {
  absoluteUrl,
  AUTHOR_NAME,
  CONTACT_EMAIL,
  PUBLISHER_NAME,
  SITE_NAME,
} from '../config/site';
import { supportingJsonLd } from '../lib/schema';

const title = 'Privacy on the Morse Code Translator: Data Stays in Browser';
const description =
  'Privacy notes for this Morse code translator: your text stays in the browser, no cookies or analytics today, and how share links and hosting logs work.';
const pageUrl = absoluteUrl('/privacy/');
const lastUpdated = '28 November 2026';
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: absoluteUrl('/') },
  { name: 'Privacy', url: pageUrl },
];
const jsonLd = supportingJsonLd({
  name: 'Privacy',
  description,
  url: pageUrl,
  crumbs,
  dateModified: lastUpdatedIso('/privacy/'),
});

const link = 'text-accent underline underline-offset-4';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  suffix={false}
  image="/og/privacy.jpg"
  imageAlt="Privacy"
>
  <article class="grid max-w-3xl gap-8 text-[1.0625rem] leading-7">
    <Breadcrumb items={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home' }, { label: 'Privacy' }]} />
    <header class="grid gap-3">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Who runs this site</h2>
      <p>
        This site, {SITE_NAME}, is published by {PUBLISHER_NAME}. The founder is {AUTHOR_NAME}. You can contact us at
        <a class={link} href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What stays in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        The translator, the tap input, the Morse Code Machine and the audio and image decoders run in your browser. The
        text you type, the sounds you play or upload and the images you choose are processed on your device and are not
        uploaded to this site. When the microphone is used, its audio is not recorded, stored or sent. A file you upload
        is not stored, and closing or refreshing the page discards it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What the site stores on your device</h2>
      <p>
        The site sets no cookies of its own. It may store your light or dark theme choice in your browser's local
        storage. That value stays on your device.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Share links</h2>
      <p>
        A share link puts your text in the part of the address after the # sign. Browsers do not send that part to the
        server, but anyone who has the link can read the text. Only share links that contain text you are happy to share.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Hosting and server logs</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted behind Cloudflare. Like most hosts, Cloudflare may keep standard server logs, such as the page
        requested, the time and technical connection details. Those logs do not contain what you type into the tools. See
        <a class={link} href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare's own privacy policy</a>
        for how long logs are kept.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Video</h2>
      <p>
        The demo video on the home page uses the YouTube privacy-enhanced player. Nothing is requested from YouTube until
        you press play. The American Morse page uses the same privacy-enhanced player as a lazy-loaded iframe, so YouTube
        may be requested when that part of the page is shown, not only after a play click.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Emails you send us</h2>
      <p>
        If you email {CONTACT_EMAIL}, we receive your email address and what you write. We use it only to reply to you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Analytics and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        At the time of this update, this site does not load analytics, advertising or social media tracking scripts. This
        section will be replaced on the day analytics or ads are switched on. It will then name the services, say what
        data they collect and link to their own policies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We update the date at the top of this page when this policy changes. The date at the top shows when this page was
        last updated.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
